# Vendored third-party code

## `basis_transcoder.wasm`

- Source: Basis Universal transcoder, Binomial LLC
  (https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal), Apache License 2.0
  (https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal/blob/master/LICENSE).
- Revision: `ad9386a4a1cf2a248f7bbd45f543a7448db15267` (v1.16.4-16-gad9386a).
  This is the exact tree vendored by the native `basis-universal` 0.3.1 crate,
  so the web transcoder and the native codec transcode the same payload to the
  same bytes.
- Built by classic-wgl (see `build.sh` + `transcoder_wrapper.cpp`): an
  Emscripten build (6.0.2, via the flake's pinned nixpkgs) of
  `transcoder/basisu_transcoder.cpp` (transcoder-only, no encoder) plus our
  `transcoder_wrapper.cpp` C ABI (`classic_initialize` / `classic_transcode`),
  exposing the full `transcoder_texture_format` set — including
  `ETC2_EAC_R11` / `ETC2_EAC_RG11` for single-channel depth.

The wasm is a standalone module (no Emscripten JS runtime); `bootstrap.js` /
`transcoder_worker.js` are our own glue, not third-party code.

